From 1e957fbe5789b6ac4a3e8c00657d2699c4b61e15 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert Wojciechowski <24755+wojo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:03:01 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] GLM on CUDA: --learn-conversations keeps every rank's part of a kept state on disk

Rank 0's engine thread leases, fills, reads and seals each rank's copy through the follow link
(cuda_disk_ranks: blank, put, take, seal, prefixes). The store's image is rank 0's image followed by
each other rank's prefix, the one part a rank holds alone; the rest are the same bytes on every rank,
checked at start by the identity probe. A blank state is refused by restore until its seal.

A blank whose disk step fails on the link gives rank 0's lease back, and its id goes on the dropped
list, so the next step drops it on any rank the step reached; the id is not used again. An NCCL failure
there already ends every rank (the liveness lines), but a CUDA error in the step's launch or upload
returns to the disk read, which tries one shorter state and then prefills while the server goes on.
cuda_disk_ranks_test.zig runs the steps on host memory with a fake link: that failed blank, a blank state
refusing bytes past its words and front until sealed (DiskOrder), each BadStep a follower refuses before
its states or the link, and each other rank's shared bytes taken past its prefix and compared to rank 0's
(RanksDiffer, in ranks.same, which the probe calls). attach's refusals of the shared store and of more
ranks than prefix_buf holds (KvShareWithLearnConversations, TooManyRanks) have their own test in
cuda_glm_disk.zig. link and prefix_buf stay process-wide: the process serves one model.
With TF_GLM_KV_LIVE_HALF=1 a keep holds one KDA half and the disk image both, so GLM refuses
--learn-conversations with it by name at startup (cuda_refusal.zig); the test that pinned GLM refusing
--learn-conversations outright now pins that it takes the flag alone and refuses it beside live-half keeps.

Rank 0's link becomes the disk steps' link in `follow.Link.lead` (which also sets whether the other ranks begin
asleep), at TP only, and `Link.deinit` clears it, so cuda_native.zig stays at its 600 lines. cuda_disk_ranks_test.zig:
one rank leaves the steps local, two set the link, another link's deinit leaves it, its own clears it; the test fails
with the clear removed.
---

